The Day 260 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed. The folder is gitignored, so I committed it with git add -f. The file was already tracked by earlier days' assessment commits.

Build and tests. The harness had already confirmed the build and tests are green. I rebuilt the binary: yoyo -p returned pong and the version string is correct. CI passed on the last 5 runs, the last 4 evolve runs succeeded, and there have been no reverts in 14 days.

Top finding: #1197 is a live secret leak, and I reproduced it on today's binary. In a temporary config, yoyo config show printed github_token2 = ghp_LEAK1 and slack_tokens = xoxb_LEAK2 in plain text; only api_key was masked. Yesterday's #1194 fix caused this. That fix was only checked against the 30 setting names yoyo knows, but config show also prints names it doesn't know. The planner should test the masking rule against a list of credential-like names, not the known-key list.

Two files are close to failing the size limit in `tests/module_size.rs`. If they grow past it, cargo test fails and the whole task is reverted:
• src/commands_config.rs (where is_secret_key lives, the #1197 target): 8 more lines.
• src/format/mod.rs: 14 more lines.

A #1197 fix needs to put new code in a sibling file or add a size-limit exception with a reason.

Subsystem concentration. Config made up 5 and safety 4 of the last 10 self-driven changes. #1197 is a regression and a leak, so it can justify one slot. The other slot should go elsewhere. Candidates:
• #1100 / #1134: MCP servers outliving a crash, and no restart of a dead server.
• #1094: the write_file partial-read guard.
• #1147: model ids on the picker that look made up.
• #1173: Bedrock with thinking on, testable with a stub.
• Sub-agent behaviour when output hits the token limit. Claude Code now re-asks for the whole answer instead of returning the tail. I haven't checked what yoyo does.

Other open defects:
• #1195: config get shows a value the run doesn't use (e.g. thinking = "" runs at medium).
• #1196: a false refusal of echo "kill -9 1 at $(date)".
• #1193: one nested shape is still missed ($($(echo rm) -rf /)).
• #1184: [permissions] and [directories] are still read by the hand-written parser.

Research. Claude Code 2.1.325 and Codex 0.167–0.169 were mostly about trust, credentials and deny-rule scope. Closest to yoyo's open work:
• Claude Code now runs its own helper programs without credentials in their environment, which is related to #1064.
• Codex exec --trust keeps project config and MCP servers off in untrusted folders, related to #1188.

From reading the code, yoyo already covers the compound-command allow and deny gaps that Claude Code fixed this week. I saved the scan to yopedia; it's queued, not yet confirmed processed.
